- content_for :title, "Knowledge formatting guide - Admin"

.flex.max-w-7xl.mx-auto.px-4.sm:px-6.lg:px-8.py-8.gap-8
  = render "sidebar", current_page: nil
  .flex-1.min-w-0
    .bg-white.rounded-xl.shadow.border.border-gray-100.overflow-hidden
      .px-6.py-4.border-b.border-gray-100.flex.flex-wrap.items-center.justify-between.gap-3
        div
          h1.text-2xl.font-bold.text-gray-900 Knowledge formatting guide
          p.text-sm.text-gray-600.mt-1 How to write pages, use the editor, and link between them.
        = link_to "All pages", admin_wiki_pages_path, class: "px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 text-sm text-gray-700 rounded-md hover:bg-gray-50"

      .px-6.py-8.prose.max-w-none.text-gray-800
        h2.text-xl.font-semibold.text-gray-900 Editor (Trix)

        p
          | The content area is a rich text editor. Use the toolbar for
          strong  bold
          | ,
          em  italic
          | , headings, bullet and numbered lists, quotes, code, links, and file attachments (images and documents upload through the paperclip icon).

        p
          strong  External links:
          |  Use the link button and paste a full URL (
          code.text-sm https://…
          | ). Those open like normal web links.

        h2.text-xl.font-semibold.text-gray-900.mt-10 Internal wiki links

        p
          | To point readers at another knowledge page
          strong  without typing the site URL
          | , use double square brackets. The site turns these into links when someone
          strong  views
          |  the page (they stay as plain text while you edit).

        h3.text-lg.font-semibold.text-gray-900.mt-6 Page addresses

        p
          | Each page has a path built from its parent chain and slug, for example a URL ending with
          code.text-sm
            | /en/admin/knowledge/boards/baldrick8
          |  for a page with slug
          code.text-sm baldrick8
          |  under a parent whose slug is
          code.text-sm boards
          | . Root pages use a single segment (just their slug).

        h3.text-lg.font-semibold.text-gray-900.mt-6 Syntax

        table.w-full.text-sm.border-collapse.my-4
          thead
            tr.border-b.border-gray-200
              th.text-left.py-2.pr-4 Write
              th.text-left.py-2 Meaning
          tbody
            tr.border-b.border-gray-100
              td.py-2.pr-4
                code.bg-gray-100.rounded.px-1.5.py-0.5
                  | [[parent-slug/child-slug]]
              td.py-2
                | Link using the full path when you need a specific nested page (same order as in the browser address bar, omitting the locale and
                code.text-xs
                  | /admin/knowledge/
                | prefix).
            tr.border-b.border-gray-100
              td.py-2.pr-4
                code.bg-gray-100.rounded.px-1.5.py-0.5
                  | [[page-slug]]
              td.py-2
                | Link using the target page’s
                strong slug
                |  (shown under the title when you view that page). Slugs only need to be unique among siblings; use a path row above when the same slug exists under different parents.
            tr.border-b.border-gray-100
              td.py-2.pr-4
                code.bg-gray-100.rounded.px-1.5.py-0.5
                  | [[Page title]]
              td.py-2
                | Link by
                strong title
                | , case-insensitive. If two pages share the same title, the first match wins—prefer a slug in that case.
            tr.border-b.border-gray-100
              td.py-2.pr-4
                code.bg-gray-100.rounded.px-1.5.py-0.5
                  | [[slug|Label shown]]
              td.py-2
                | Same as a slug or title link, but the visible text is
                strong Label shown
                |  (MediaWiki-style:
                code.text-xs
                  | target|label
                | ).

        h3.text-lg.font-semibold.text-gray-900.mt-6 Where markers work

        ul.list-disc.pl-5.space-y-1
          li Normal paragraphs and most body text.
          li
            strong Not
            |  expanded inside preformatted or code blocks, inside existing hyperlinks, or in a few other special regions—so you can show literal
            code.bg-gray-100.rounded.px-1
              | [[brackets]]
            |  in examples if you put them in a preformatted block.

        h3.text-lg.font-semibold.text-gray-900.mt-6 Broken links

        p
          | If nothing matches the name you put in the brackets, the text still appears but styled as a
          strong  dotted warning
          |  line; hover for a short explanation. Fix the slug or title, or create the missing page.

        h2.text-xl.font-semibold.text-gray-900.mt-10 Page tree

        ul.list-disc.pl-5.space-y-1
          li
            strong  Parent page
            |  — choose a parent to nest this page under the sidebar. Leave as “Top level” for a root page.
          li
            strong  Position
            |  — lower numbers sort earlier among siblings in the sidebar.

        p.mt-6
          = link_to "Back to knowledge home", admin_wiki_pages_path, class: "text-indigo-600 font-medium hover:text-indigo-800"
